WEBVTT

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:34.937
<i>Kristin: hey, meredith, it's kristin.</i>

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.137
<i>You have to tell me
what happened last night.</i>

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:38.137
<i>Call me.</i>

00:03:39.337 --> 00:03:41.471
<i>Brad: hey, meredith. Brad calling.</i>

00:03:41.504 --> 00:03:44.304
<i>Listen, do you want to hook up later?</i>

00:03:44.337 --> 00:03:47.671
<i>Well, i'll talk to you
then. Give me a call. Thanks.</i>

00:03:52.271 --> 00:03:54.738
<i>Brock: hey, meredith, what's
going on? This is brock.</i>

00:03:54.770 --> 00:03:57.571
<i>I just wanted to let you know
the gang is gonna get together.</i>

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.404
<i>We're gonna go to the garage.</i>

00:03:59.437 --> 00:04:01.437
<i>We're gonna have some
beers and some shots.</i>

00:04:31.970 --> 00:04:34.937
All right, dean, this is the place.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.937
I've got to say dad and me did just fine

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:39.304
Without these stupid costumes.

00:04:39.337 --> 00:04:42.638
I feel like a
high-School-Drama dork.

00:04:44.504 --> 00:04:46.471
What was that play that you did?

00:04:46.504 --> 00:04:48.304
What was it
-- "Our town"?

00:04:48.337 --> 00:04:49.970
Yeah, you were good. It was cute.

00:04:50.004 --> 00:04:51.803
Look, you want to pull this off or not?

00:04:51.837 --> 00:04:54.337
I'm just saying these outfits
cost hard-Earned money.

00:04:54.371 --> 00:04:55.437
Whose?

00:04:55.471 --> 00:04:58.803
Ours. You think
credit-Card fraud is easy?

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.037
Thanks for letting us look around.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:06.571
The police said they were
done with the place, so...

00:05:17.204 --> 00:05:19.337
You guys said you were
with the alarm company?

00:05:19.371 --> 00:05:20.704
That's right.

00:05:20.738 --> 00:05:22.004
Well, no offense,

00:05:22.037 --> 00:05:25.170
But your alarm is about as
useful as boobs on a man.

00:05:25.204 --> 00:05:27.170
Well, that's
why we're here --

00:05:27.204 --> 00:05:30.537
To see what went wrong, to
stop it from happening again.

00:05:32.571 --> 00:05:34.371
Now, ma'am, you found the body?

00:05:34.404 --> 00:05:35.537
Yeah.

00:05:35.571 --> 00:05:36.870
Right after it happened?

00:05:36.903 --> 00:05:38.204
No, a few days later.

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:40.870
Meredith's work called.
She hadn't showed up.

00:05:40.903 --> 00:05:42.970
I knocked on her door.

00:05:43.004 --> 00:05:45.937
That's when i noticed... the smell.

00:05:45.970 --> 00:05:49.404
Any windows open? Any sign of break-In?

00:05:49.437 --> 00:05:50.870
Windows were locked.
Front door was bolted.

00:05:50.903 --> 00:05:53.271
Chain was on the door. We
had to cut it to get in.

00:05:53.304 --> 00:05:54.604
And the alarm was still on?

00:05:54.638 --> 00:05:57.604
Like i said. Bang-Up job
your company is doing.

00:05:57.638 --> 00:05:59.704
Did you see any overturned furniture,

00:05:59.738 --> 00:06:01.371
Broken glass, signs of struggle?

00:06:01.404 --> 00:06:04.337
Everything was in perfect condition...

00:06:04.371 --> 00:06:06.271
Except meredith.

00:06:06.304 --> 00:06:09.437
Well, what condition was meredith in?

00:06:09.471 --> 00:06:12.837
Meredith was all over, in pieces.

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.704
The guy who killed her
must have been a whack job.

00:06:15.738 --> 00:06:18.304
But i tell you, if i
didn't know any better,

00:06:18.337 --> 00:06:20.537
I'd have said a wild animal did it.

00:06:23.571 --> 00:06:26.170
Ma'am, you mind if we take some time,

00:06:26.204 --> 00:06:28.271
Give this place a once-Over?

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:31.704
Go right ahead. Knock yourself out.

00:06:37.104 --> 00:06:39.237
So the killer walks in
and out of the apartment --

00:06:39.271 --> 00:06:40.738
No weapons, no prints, nothing.

00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:43.070
I'm telling you, the
minute i found that article,

00:06:43.104 --> 00:06:44.738
I knew this was our kind of gig.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.271
I think i agree with you.

00:06:46.304 --> 00:06:48.770
So, you talked to the cops?

00:06:48.803 --> 00:06:52.304
Uh, yeah, i
spoke to amy --

00:06:52.337 --> 00:06:56.304
A, uh, charming, perky
officer of the law.

00:06:56.337 --> 00:06:57.638
What did you find out?

00:06:57.671 --> 00:07:00.638
Well, she's a sagittarius.
She loves tequila.

00:07:00.671 --> 00:07:02.837
I mean...whew.

00:07:02.870 --> 00:07:05.004
Oh, and she's got this
little tattoo. Dean!

00:07:05.037 --> 00:07:06.170
What? Yeah.

00:07:06.204 --> 00:07:08.004
Nothing we don't already know,

00:07:08.037 --> 00:07:11.304
Except for one thing they're
keeping out of the papers.

00:07:11.337 --> 00:07:12.770
Meredith's heart was missing.

00:07:14.604 --> 00:07:15.738
Her heart?

00:07:15.770 --> 00:07:18.237
Yeah, her heart.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:20.070
So, what do you think did it to her?

00:07:20.104 --> 00:07:22.471
The landlady said it looked
like an animal attack.

00:07:22.504 --> 00:07:25.371
Maybe it was. Werewolf?

00:07:25.404 --> 00:07:27.271
Not a werewolf. The
lunar cycle's not right.

00:07:27.304 --> 00:07:28.337
If it was a creature,

00:07:28.371 --> 00:07:30.137
It would've left some kind of trace.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:33.803
It was probably a spirit.

00:07:33.837 --> 00:07:35.937
Hmm.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:39.471
See if you can find
any masking tape around.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.371
Ever see that symbol before?

00:08:04.404 --> 00:08:06.837
Never.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:08.837
Me, neither.

00:08:42.204 --> 00:08:44.504
I talked to the bartender.

00:08:44.537 --> 00:08:46.937
Did you get anything...
besides her number?

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.803
Dude, i'm a professional.
I'm offended that...

00:08:52.437 --> 00:08:55.037
All right.

00:08:55.070 --> 00:08:57.237
You mind doing a little bit of thinking

00:08:57.271 --> 00:08:59.070
With your upstairs brain, dean?

00:08:59.104 --> 00:09:00.803
Hmm? There's nothing to find out.

00:09:00.837 --> 00:09:02.837
Meredith worked here. She waited tables.

00:09:02.870 --> 00:09:05.371
Everyone here is her friend.
Everyone says she's normal.

00:09:05.404 --> 00:09:07.704
She didn't do or say anything
weird before she died.

00:09:07.738 --> 00:09:09.970
What about that symbol?
Did you find anything?

00:09:10.004 --> 00:09:11.371
Nope. Nothing.

00:09:11.404 --> 00:09:13.870
It wasn't in dad's journal
or in any of the usual books.

00:09:13.903 --> 00:09:16.638
I just have to dig a
little deeper, i guess.

00:09:16.671 --> 00:09:20.037
There was a first victim,
right, before meredith?

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:22.037
Right, yeah. His name was, uh...

00:09:22.070 --> 00:09:24.070
His name was ben swardstrom.

00:09:24.104 --> 00:09:26.738
Last month he was found
mutilated in his town house.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:29.803
Same deal. The door was
locked. The alarm was on.

00:09:29.837 --> 00:09:31.738
Is there any connection between them?

00:09:31.770 --> 00:09:33.070
Nothing i could tell.

00:09:33.104 --> 00:09:35.104
Ben was a banker.
Meredith was a waitress.

00:09:35.137 --> 00:09:37.204
They never met, never
knew anyone in common.

00:09:37.237 --> 00:09:39.571
They were practically
from different worlds.

00:09:39.604 --> 00:09:41.404
So the only successful
intel we've scored

00:09:41.437 --> 00:09:44.104
Is the bartender's phone number.

00:09:45.204 --> 00:09:47.404
What?

00:09:50.437 --> 00:09:51.604
Sam?

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:01.104
Meg.

00:10:01.137 --> 00:10:02.704
Sam!

00:10:06.970 --> 00:10:11.170
Sam, is that you? Oh, my gosh!

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:15.970
What are you doing here?

00:10:16.003 --> 00:10:17.937
I'm just in town
-- Visiting friends.

00:10:19.903 --> 00:10:21.037
Where are they?

00:10:21.070 --> 00:10:23.371
Well, they're not here right now,

00:10:23.404 --> 00:10:24.970
But what about you, meg?

00:10:25.003 --> 00:10:26.838
I thought you were going to california.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:28.170
Oh, i did.

00:10:28.204 --> 00:10:30.371
I came. I saw. I conquered.

00:10:30.404 --> 00:10:32.903
Oh, and i met
what's his name --

00:10:32.937 --> 00:10:35.404
Something michael
murray -- At a bar.

00:10:35.437 --> 00:10:36.571
Who?

00:10:36.604 --> 00:10:37.838
It doesn't matter.

00:10:37.870 --> 00:10:40.237
Anyway, the whole scene got old,

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:42.537
So i'm living here for a while.

00:10:43.771 --> 00:10:45.070
You're from chicago?

00:10:45.104 --> 00:10:48.070
No, massachusetts
-- Andover.

00:10:48.104 --> 00:10:49.637
Gosh, sam,

00:10:49.671 --> 00:10:51.838
What are the odds we'd
run into each other?

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:53.838
I know. I thought i'd
never see you again.

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:56.104
Well, i'm glad you were wrong.

00:10:59.537 --> 00:11:01.537
Dude, cover your mouth.

00:11:01.571 --> 00:11:04.437
Yeah, i'm sorry, meg.

00:11:04.471 --> 00:11:07.671
This is, um -- This
is my brother, dean.

00:11:09.704 --> 00:11:10.903
This is dean?

00:11:10.937 --> 00:11:12.704
Yeah. So you've heard of me?

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:14.537
Oh, yeah, i've heard of you.

00:11:14.571 --> 00:11:18.337
Nice -- The way you treat
your brother like luggage.

00:11:18.371 --> 00:11:19.671
Sorry?

00:11:19.704 --> 00:11:22.270
Why don't you let him
do what he wants to do?

00:11:22.304 --> 00:11:24.704
Stop dragging him
over god's green earth.

00:11:24.738 --> 00:11:26.903
Meg...it's all right.

00:11:29.237 --> 00:11:32.371
Okay. Awkward.

00:11:32.404 --> 00:11:35.437
I'm gonna get a drink now.

00:11:40.003 --> 00:11:41.304
Sam, i'm sorry.

00:11:41.337 --> 00:11:46.003
It's just, the way you
told me he treats you,

00:11:46.037 --> 00:11:47.870
If it were me, i'd kill him.

00:11:47.903 --> 00:11:49.404
It's all right. He means well.

00:11:49.437 --> 00:11:52.037
We should hook up while you're in town.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.204
Yeah.

00:11:53.237 --> 00:11:55.237
I could show you a hell of a time.

00:11:55.270 --> 00:11:56.537
That sounds great.

00:11:56.571 --> 00:11:58.537
Why don't you give me your number?

00:11:58.571 --> 00:12:01.870

312-555-0143.

00:12:01.903 --> 00:12:03.738
You know what? I never
got your last name.

00:12:03.771 --> 00:12:05.371
Masters. Masters?

00:12:05.404 --> 00:12:06.604
So you better call.

00:12:06.637 --> 00:12:08.604
Scout's honor.

00:12:08.637 --> 00:12:12.637
I hope to see you around, sam.

00:12:22.137 --> 00:12:23.437
Who the hell we he?

00:12:23.471 --> 00:12:25.437
I don't really know.
I only met her once.

00:12:25.471 --> 00:12:27.771
Meeting up with her again?

00:12:27.804 --> 00:12:31.104
I don't know, man. It's weird.

00:12:31.137 --> 00:12:33.771
What was she saying --
I treat you like luggage?

00:12:33.804 --> 00:12:35.771
Were you bitching
about me to some chick?

00:12:35.804 --> 00:12:37.104
Look, i'm sorry, dean.

00:12:37.137 --> 00:12:38.604
It was when we had that huge fight

00:12:38.637 --> 00:12:40.637
When i was in the bus stop in indiana.

00:12:40.671 --> 00:12:42.637
Is there any truth to what she's saying?

00:12:42.671 --> 00:12:44.504
Am i keeping you against your will, sam?

00:12:44.537 --> 00:12:46.437
No, of course not.
Now, would you listen?

00:12:46.471 --> 00:12:48.437
What?!

00:12:48.471 --> 00:12:50.937
I think there's something
strange going on here, dean.

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.571
Tell me about it. She
wasn't even into me.

00:12:52.604 --> 00:12:55.137
No, man, i mean, like
our kind of strange.

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:57.137
Maybe even a lead. Why do you say that?

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:59.937
I met meg weeks ago literally
on the side of the road.

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:02.237
Now i run into her in
some random chicago bar --

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.771
The same bar where a waitress

00:13:03.804 --> 00:13:05.838
Was slaughtered by
something supernatural.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:07.804
You don't think that's
weird? It happens.

00:13:07.838 --> 00:13:09.870
Well, yeah, it happens, but not to us.

00:13:09.903 --> 00:13:11.104
Look, i could be wrong.

00:13:11.137 --> 00:13:13.471
I'm just saying there's
something about this girl

00:13:13.504 --> 00:13:15.137
That i can't quite put my finger on.

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.804
But i bet you'd like to.

00:13:16.838 --> 00:13:18.504
But maybe she's not a suspect.

00:13:18.537 --> 00:13:20.437
Maybe you got a thing for her, huh?

00:13:20.471 --> 00:13:23.771
You're thinking too much
with your upstairs brain, huh?

00:13:23.804 --> 00:13:25.838
Do me a favor.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:29.037
Check and see if there's a
meg masters from massachusetts

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.504
And see if you can't dig
anything up on that symbol.

00:13:31.537 --> 00:13:32.970
What are you gonna do?

00:13:33.003 --> 00:13:34.771
I'm gonna watch meg.

00:13:34.804 --> 00:13:36.204
Yeah.

00:13:36.237 --> 00:13:37.771
I just want to see what's what.

00:13:37.804 --> 00:13:39.304
All right, you little pervert.

00:13:39.337 --> 00:13:41.337
I'm going. I'm going.

00:14:05.504 --> 00:14:06.804
Hey.

00:14:06.838 --> 00:14:08.704
You're lurking outside
that poor girl's apartment,

00:14:08.738 --> 00:14:10.504
Aren't you? No.

00:14:12.037 --> 00:14:13.838
Yes.

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:15.970
You've got a funny way
of showing your affection.

00:14:16.003 --> 00:14:18.671
You find anything on her or what?

00:14:18.704 --> 00:14:20.671
There's a meg masters in
the andover phone book.

00:14:20.704 --> 00:14:22.704
I even pulled up her high-School photo.

00:14:22.738 --> 00:14:24.870
Now, look, why don't
you go knock on her door

00:14:24.903 --> 00:14:27.204
And invite her to a poetry reading

00:14:27.237 --> 00:14:29.704
Or whatever it is you do, huh?

00:14:29.738 --> 00:14:31.771
What about the symbol? Any luck?

00:14:31.804 --> 00:14:34.070
Yeah, that i did have some luck with.

00:14:34.104 --> 00:14:38.070
Turns out it's zoroastrian.

00:14:38.104 --> 00:14:40.937
Very, very old-School, like
2,000 years before christ.

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:42.437
It's a sigil for a daeva.

00:14:42.471 --> 00:14:43.903
What's a daeva?

00:14:43.937 --> 00:14:45.903
It translates to
"demon of darkness" --

00:14:45.937 --> 00:14:48.237
Zoroastrian demons, and
they're savage, animalistic,

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:52.070
Nasty attitudes -- Kind
of like demonic pit bulls.

00:14:52.104 --> 00:14:54.270
How did you figure that out?

00:14:54.304 --> 00:14:56.404
You don't have a corner on
paper chasing around here.

00:14:56.437 --> 00:14:57.870
Name the last book you read.

00:14:59.903 --> 00:15:02.371
I called dad's friend
caleb. He told me, all right.

00:15:02.404 --> 00:15:03.804
Anyway, here's the thing.

00:15:03.838 --> 00:15:06.070
These daevas, they have to be summoned.

00:15:06.104 --> 00:15:07.771
So someone's controlling it?

00:15:07.804 --> 00:15:09.270
Yeah, that's what i'm saying.

00:15:09.304 --> 00:15:11.804
And from what i gather, it's
pretty risky business, too.

00:15:11.838 --> 00:15:14.237
These suckers tend to bite
the hand that feeds them...

00:15:14.270 --> 00:15:16.771
And the arms and the torsos.

00:15:16.804 --> 00:15:17.970
What do they look like?

00:15:18.003 --> 00:15:20.137
Nobody's seen them for
a couple of millennia.

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:21.771
Summoning a demon that ancient,

00:15:21.804 --> 00:15:23.504
Someone really knows their stuff.

00:15:23.537 --> 00:15:25.371
I think we've got a
major player in town.

00:15:26.838 --> 00:15:29.471
Why don't you go give that
girl a private strip-O-Gram?

00:15:29.504 --> 00:15:31.270
<i>Bite me. Bite her.</i>

00:15:31.304 --> 00:15:33.170
Don't leave teeth marks, though.

00:15:33.204 --> 00:15:35.170
Sam? Are
you --

00:16:04.337 --> 00:16:05.704
No, no,
i'm just --

00:16:05.738 --> 00:16:07.604
Pervert!

00:16:07.637 --> 00:16:10.237
What a creep!

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:06.571
I don't think you should come

00:19:06.604 --> 00:19:09.404
Because the brothers
-- They're in town.

00:19:09.437 --> 00:19:11.104
I didn't
know that --

00:19:16.237 --> 00:19:17.537
Yes, sir.

00:19:17.571 --> 00:19:23.037
Yes, i'll be here... waiting for you.

00:20:47.337 --> 00:20:50.471
What the hell?

00:20:55.971 --> 00:20:58.603
Dude, i've got to talk to you.

00:20:58.637 --> 00:21:00.804
So, hot little meg is
summoning the daeva?

00:21:00.837 --> 00:21:03.071
It looks like she was
using that black altar

00:21:03.104 --> 00:21:04.404
To control the thing.

00:21:04.438 --> 00:21:06.737
So sammy's got a thing for the bad girl.

00:21:06.770 --> 00:21:08.704
And what's the deal
with that bowl again?

00:21:08.737 --> 00:21:10.537
She was talking
into it --

00:21:10.570 --> 00:21:12.670
The way witches used to
scry into crystal balls.

00:21:12.704 --> 00:21:14.304
She was communicating with someone.

00:21:14.338 --> 00:21:16.971
With the daeva? No, you said
those things were savages.

00:21:17.004 --> 00:21:19.271
No, this was someone different,

00:21:19.304 --> 00:21:21.603
Someone who's giving her orders,

00:21:21.637 --> 00:21:24.371
Someone who's coming to that warehouse.

00:21:33.371 --> 00:21:34.503
Holy crap.

00:21:34.537 --> 00:21:35.971
What?

00:21:36.004 --> 00:21:37.971
What i was gonna tell you earlier.

00:21:38.004 --> 00:21:40.470
I pulled a favor with my

00:21:40.503 --> 00:21:42.937
Friend amy over at
the police department.

00:21:42.971 --> 00:21:45.503
Complete records of the two victims.

00:21:45.537 --> 00:21:47.237
We missed something the first time.

00:21:47.271 --> 00:21:49.904
What?

00:21:49.937 --> 00:21:53.438
The first victim
-- The old man?

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:55.804
He spent his whole life in chicago,

00:21:55.837 --> 00:21:58.570
But look where he was
born. Lawrence, kansas.

00:21:58.603 --> 00:21:59.904
Mm-Hmm.

00:21:59.937 --> 00:22:01.804
Meredith -- The
second victim?

00:22:01.837 --> 00:22:03.637
It turns out she was adopted.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.470
And guess where she's from?

00:22:12.837 --> 00:22:13.971
Holy crap.

00:22:14.004 --> 00:22:15.304
Yeah.

00:22:15.338 --> 00:22:17.570
I mean, that is where
the demon killed mom.

00:22:19.304 --> 00:22:20.971
You think meg's tied up with the demon?

00:22:21.004 --> 00:22:23.438
I think it's a definite possibility.

00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:25.971
What's the significance of lawrence?

00:22:26.004 --> 00:22:27.637
And how do these daeva things fit in?

00:22:27.670 --> 00:22:29.971
I say we trash that
black altar, grab meg,

00:22:30.004 --> 00:22:32.737
And have ourselves a
friendly little interrogation.

00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:34.603
No, we can't. We shouldn't tip her off.

00:22:34.637 --> 00:22:36.737
We've got to stake out that warehouse.

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:39.570
We've got to see who...or
what is showing up to meet her.

00:22:39.603 --> 00:22:40.904
I'll tell you one thing.

00:22:40.937 --> 00:22:43.603
I don't think we should do this alone.

00:22:46.004 --> 00:22:47.470
We think we've got a serious lead

00:22:47.503 --> 00:22:49.137
On the thing that killed mom.

00:22:49.171 --> 00:22:55.304
So, uh, this warehouse
-- It's 1435 west erie.

00:22:55.338 --> 00:22:56.971
Dad, if you get this,

00:22:57.004 --> 00:22:59.837
Get to chicago as soon as you can.

00:22:59.870 --> 00:23:01.503
Voice mail?

00:23:01.537 --> 00:23:02.837
Yeah.

00:23:04.037 --> 00:23:05.503
Jeez. What'd you get?

00:23:05.537 --> 00:23:08.603
I ransacked
that trunk --

00:23:08.637 --> 00:23:11.104
Holy water, y weapon
that i could think of.

00:23:11.137 --> 00:23:14.537
Exorcism rituals from about
a half-Dozen religions.

00:23:14.570 --> 00:23:17.637
I'm not sure what to expect,

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:20.603
So i guess we should just
expect everything, huh?

00:23:28.704 --> 00:23:31.338
It's a big night.

00:23:31.371 --> 00:23:33.937
Yeah.

00:23:33.971 --> 00:23:35.237
You nervous?

00:23:35.271 --> 00:23:38.770
No. No, are you?

00:23:38.804 --> 00:23:40.971
No. No way.

00:23:49.371 --> 00:23:51.171
God, could you imagine if we actually

00:23:51.204 --> 00:23:52.870
Found that damn thing, that demon?

00:23:52.904 --> 00:23:54.971
Let's not get ahead of
ourselves, all right?

00:23:55.004 --> 00:23:59.770
I know. I'm just
saying... what if we did?

00:23:59.804 --> 00:24:02.804
What if this whole
thing was over tonight?

00:24:02.837 --> 00:24:04.971
Man, i'd sleep for a month,

00:24:05.004 --> 00:24:08.837
Go back to school,
just be a person again.

00:24:08.870 --> 00:24:10.904
You want to go back to school?

00:24:10.937 --> 00:24:13.537
Yeah, once we're done hunting the thing.

00:24:14.704 --> 00:24:17.271
Why? Is there something wrong with that?

00:24:17.304 --> 00:24:21.037
No, no, it's great. Good for you.

00:24:21.071 --> 00:24:24.637
I mean, what are you gonna
do when it's all over?

00:24:24.670 --> 00:24:26.770
It's never gonna be over.

00:24:26.804 --> 00:24:28.071
There's gonna be others.

00:24:28.104 --> 00:24:30.371
There's always gonna
be something to hunt.

00:24:30.404 --> 00:24:33.204
But there's got to be something
that you want for yourself.

00:24:33.237 --> 00:24:35.637
I don't want you to leave
the second this is over.

00:24:35.670 --> 00:24:39.537
Dude, what's your problem?

00:24:45.503 --> 00:24:48.503
Why do you think i drag
you everywhere, huh?

00:24:48.537 --> 00:24:51.737
Why do you think i came
and got you at stanford?

00:24:51.770 --> 00:24:54.004
'Cause dad was in trouble.

00:24:54.037 --> 00:24:56.670
'Cause you wanted to find
the thing that killed mom.

00:24:56.704 --> 00:24:58.837
Yes, that, but it's more than that, man.

00:25:05.371 --> 00:25:10.004
You and me
and dad --

00:25:10.037 --> 00:25:13.404
I want us to be together again.

00:25:15.371 --> 00:25:19.670
I want us to be a family again.

00:25:19.704 --> 00:25:24.371
<i>Dean, we are a family.
I'd do anything for you.</i>

00:25:24.404 --> 00:25:27.404
But things will never be
the way they were before.

00:25:33.004 --> 00:25:35.670
They could be.

00:25:39.371 --> 00:25:41.037
I don't want them to be.

00:25:45.204 --> 00:25:47.204
I'm not gonna live this life forever.

00:25:47.237 --> 00:25:50.570
Dean, when this is all over,

00:25:50.603 --> 00:25:53.837
You're gonna have to
let me go my own way.

00:26:56.603 --> 00:27:00.870
Guys. Hiding is a little bit
childish, don't you think?

00:27:00.904 --> 00:27:02.870
That didn't work out like i'd planned.

00:27:05.804 --> 00:27:05.904
Why don't you come out?

00:27:16.071 --> 00:27:19.570
Sam, i have to say,

00:27:19.603 --> 00:27:22.304
This puts a real crimp
in our relationship.

00:27:22.338 --> 00:27:24.171
Yeah, tell me about it.

00:27:24.204 --> 00:27:26.870
So, where's your little daeva friend?

00:27:26.904 --> 00:27:28.104
Around.

00:27:28.137 --> 00:27:30.770
And that shotgun's
not gonna do much good.

00:27:30.804 --> 00:27:32.704
Oh, don't worry, sweetheart.

00:27:32.737 --> 00:27:34.237
The shotgun's not for the demon.

00:27:34.271 --> 00:27:37.837
So, who is it, meg? Who's coming?

00:27:37.870 --> 00:27:39.338
Who are you waiting for?

00:27:39.371 --> 00:27:41.870
You.

00:28:12.121 --> 00:28:15.287
Hey, sam, don't take this the wrong way,

00:28:15.321 --> 00:28:18.653
But your girlfriend... is a bitch.

00:28:18.687 --> 00:28:22.854
This, the whole thing, was a trap.

00:28:24.753 --> 00:28:27.387
Running into you at the bar,

00:28:27.421 --> 00:28:31.121
Following you here, hearing
what you had to say --

00:28:31.154 --> 00:28:33.187
It was all a setup, wasn't it?

00:28:34.787 --> 00:28:36.787
And that the victims were from lawrence.

00:28:36.820 --> 00:28:38.187
It doesn't mean anything.

00:28:38.221 --> 00:28:40.820
It was just to draw you in, that's all.

00:28:40.854 --> 00:28:42.687
You killed those two people for nothing.

00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:44.987
Baby, i've killed a
lot more for a lot less.

00:28:46.887 --> 00:28:50.020
You trapped us. Good for you.

00:28:50.054 --> 00:28:52.354
It's miller time.

00:28:52.387 --> 00:28:54.187
Why don't you kill us already?

00:28:54.221 --> 00:28:57.321
Not very quick on the uptake, are we?

00:29:02.954 --> 00:29:04.620
This trap isn't for you.

00:29:08.488 --> 00:29:09.653
Dad.

00:29:10.820 --> 00:29:12.254
It's a trap for dad.

00:29:15.121 --> 00:29:17.954
Oh, sweetheart, you're
dumber than you look.

00:29:17.987 --> 00:29:21.920
'Cause even if dad was
in town, which he is not,

00:29:21.954 --> 00:29:23.920
He wouldn't walk into
something like this.

00:29:23.954 --> 00:29:25.653
He's too good.

00:29:25.687 --> 00:29:28.020
He is pretty good, i'll give you that.

00:29:33.020 --> 00:29:35.020
But you see

00:29:40.354 --> 00:29:42.154
He has one weakness.

00:29:42.187 --> 00:29:43.521
What's that?

00:29:43.554 --> 00:29:45.287
You.

00:29:46.687 --> 00:29:49.554
He lets his guard down around his boys,

00:29:49.588 --> 00:29:52.954
Lets his emotions cloud his judgment.

00:29:54.920 --> 00:29:57.720
<i>I happen to know he is in town,</i>

00:29:57.753 --> 00:30:02.488
And he'll come and try to save you.

00:30:02.521 --> 00:30:05.387
And then the daevas
will kill everybody --

00:30:05.421 --> 00:30:09.987
Nice and slow... and messy.

00:30:10.020 --> 00:30:12.321
Well, i've got news for you.

00:30:12.354 --> 00:30:15.653
It's gonna take a lot more
than some...shadow to kill him.

00:30:15.687 --> 00:30:17.854
Oh, the daevas are in the room here.

00:30:17.887 --> 00:30:19.087
They're invisible.

00:30:19.121 --> 00:30:21.454
Their shadows are just
the only part you can see.

00:30:21.488 --> 00:30:22.987
Why are you doing this, meg?

00:30:23.020 --> 00:30:25.221
What kind of deal you got
worked out here, huh...

00:30:25.254 --> 00:30:26.554
And with who?

00:30:26.588 --> 00:30:28.488
I'm doing this for the same reasons

00:30:28.521 --> 00:30:30.488
You do what
you do --

00:30:30.521 --> 00:30:32.854
Loyalty, love.

00:30:38.521 --> 00:30:40.488
Like the love you had for
mommy...and jess.Go to he

00:30:40.521 --> 00:30:44.054
Baby, i'm already there.

00:30:46.087 --> 00:30:48.221
Come on, sam.

00:30:48.254 --> 00:30:51.254
There's no need to be nasty.

00:30:55.753 --> 00:30:59.720
I think we both know...

00:30:59.753 --> 00:31:02.588
How you really feel about me.

00:31:06.020 --> 00:31:07.687
You know

00:31:09.753 --> 00:31:13.720
I saw you... watching me...

00:31:13.753 --> 00:31:17.287
Changing in my apartment.

00:31:17.321 --> 00:31:19.887
It turned you on, didn't it?

00:31:19.920 --> 00:31:21.920
Get a room, you two.

00:31:21.954 --> 00:31:23.454
I didn't mind.

00:31:23.488 --> 00:31:26.121
I liked that you were watching me.

00:31:26.154 --> 00:31:28.121
Come on, sammy,

00:31:28.154 --> 00:31:31.121
You and i can still
have a little dirty fun.

00:31:31.154 --> 00:31:33.753
You want to have fun? Go ahead, then.

00:31:33.787 --> 00:31:36.287
I'm a little tied up right now.

00:32:11.488 --> 00:32:14.454
Now, were you just trying to distract me

00:32:14.488 --> 00:32:17.620
While your brother cuts free?

00:32:17.653 --> 00:32:20.287
No.

00:32:20.321 --> 00:32:22.287
No.

00:32:22.321 --> 00:32:25.187
It was because i have a knife of my own.

00:32:27.887 --> 00:32:29.187
Sam!

00:32:29.221 --> 00:32:31.054
Get the altar.

00:33:10.720 --> 00:33:12.354
So, i guess the daevas

00:33:12.388 --> 00:33:14.687
Didn't like being bossed around.

00:33:14.720 --> 00:33:16.854
I guess not.

00:33:16.887 --> 00:33:18.187
Hey, sam?

00:33:18.221 --> 00:33:19.354
Hmm?

00:33:19.388 --> 00:33:21.354
Next time you want to get laid,

00:33:21.388 --> 00:33:25.054
Find a girl that's not
so buckets of crazy, huh?

00:33:39.854 --> 00:33:42.254
Why don't you just leave
that stuff in the car?

00:33:42.288 --> 00:33:44.587
I said it before, and
i'll say it again --

00:33:44.620 --> 00:33:47.787
Better safe than sorry.

00:33:51.354 --> 00:33:52.520
Hey!

00:34:05.420 --> 00:34:07.021
Dad.

00:34:07.054 --> 00:34:09.054
Hey, boys.

00:34:37.420 --> 00:34:38.553
Hi, sam.

00:34:38.587 --> 00:34:39.921
Hi, dad.

00:34:43.453 --> 00:34:45.754
Dad, it was a trap.

00:34:45.787 --> 00:34:49.420
I didn't know. I'm sorry.

00:34:49.453 --> 00:34:52.553
It's all right. I thought
it might have been.

00:34:52.587 --> 00:34:54.121
Were you there?

00:34:54.154 --> 00:34:58.487
I got there just in time to
see the girl take the swan dive.

00:34:58.520 --> 00:34:59.887
She was the bad guy, right?

00:34:59.921 --> 00:35:01.420
Yes, sir.Yes, sir.

00:35:01.453 --> 00:35:03.921
Good. Well, it doesn't surprise me.

00:35:03.954 --> 00:35:06.388
It's tried to stop me before.

00:35:06.453 --> 00:35:08.420
The demon has?

00:35:08.453 --> 00:35:11.754
It knows i'm close. It
knows i'm gonna kill it.

00:35:11.787 --> 00:35:15.354
Not just exorcise it
or send it back to hell,

00:35:15.388 --> 00:35:18.154
Actually kill it.

00:35:18.187 --> 00:35:19.754
How?

00:35:19.787 --> 00:35:22.854
I'm working on that.

00:35:22.887 --> 00:35:26.520
Let us come with you. We'll help.

00:35:26.553 --> 00:35:30.121
No, sam.

00:35:30.154 --> 00:35:31.187
Not yet.

00:35:31.221 --> 00:35:33.453
Listen, try to understand.

00:35:33.487 --> 00:35:35.921
This demon is a scary son of a bitch.

00:35:35.954 --> 00:35:38.587
I don't want you
caught in the crossfire.

00:35:38.620 --> 00:35:39.921
I don't want you hurt.

00:35:39.954 --> 00:35:42.087
You don't have to worry about us.

00:35:42.121 --> 00:35:43.121
Of course i do.

00:35:45.453 --> 00:35:47.453
I'm your father.

00:35:51.487 --> 00:35:55.787
Listen, sammy, the last
time we were together,

00:35:55.820 --> 00:35:57.620
We had one hell of a fight.

00:35:57.654 --> 00:35:58.787
Yes, sir.

00:36:06.654 --> 00:36:09.620
It's good to see you again.

00:36:09.654 --> 00:36:11.487
It's been a long time.

00:36:13.887 --> 00:36:15.221
Too long.

00:36:42.720 --> 00:36:44.221
No!

00:37:22.967 --> 00:37:24.834
These things are shadow demons,

00:37:24.867 --> 00:37:26.567
So let's light 'em up!

00:37:41.533 --> 00:37:42.667
Dad!

00:37:42.700 --> 00:37:43.901
Over here!

00:37:46.101 --> 00:37:48.334
Come on!

00:38:13.167 --> 00:38:15.467
All right, come on. We
don't have much time.

00:38:15.500 --> 00:38:17.967
As soon as the flare's
out, they'll be back.

00:38:18.001 --> 00:38:19.533
Wait, wait!

00:38:19.567 --> 00:38:21.934
Sam, wait.

00:38:25.567 --> 00:38:27.034
Dad, you can't come with us.

00:38:27.067 --> 00:38:32.268
What? What are you talking about?

00:38:32.301 --> 00:38:33.800
We'll be all right.

00:38:33.834 --> 00:38:36.600
Dean, we should stick together!
We'll go after those --

00:38:36.634 --> 00:38:37.967
Sam, listen to me!

00:38:40.901 --> 00:38:42.934
We almost got dad killed in there.

00:38:42.967 --> 00:38:45.934
Don't you understand?
They're not gonna stop.

00:38:45.967 --> 00:38:47.533
They're gonna try again.

00:38:47.567 --> 00:38:49.967
They're gonna use us to get to him.

00:38:50.001 --> 00:38:51.667
I mean, meg was right.

00:38:51.700 --> 00:38:54.500
Dad's vulnerable when he's with us.

00:38:56.101 --> 00:39:00.500
He...he's stronger without us around.

00:39:02.567 --> 00:39:04.234
Dad...

00:39:05.934 --> 00:39:07.901
No.

00:39:07.934 --> 00:39:10.034
After everything,

00:39:10.067 --> 00:39:12.800
After all the time we
spent looking for you,

00:39:12.834 --> 00:39:15.334
Please.

00:39:15.368 --> 00:39:17.101
I've got to be a part of this fight.

00:39:17.134 --> 00:39:19.101
Sammy, this fight is just starting,

00:39:19.134 --> 00:39:21.834
And we are all gonna
have a part to play.

00:39:21.867 --> 00:39:23.600
For now, you've got to trust me, son.

00:39:25.967 --> 00:39:29.901
Okay? You've got to let me go.

00:40:13.734 --> 00:40:15.867
Be careful, boys.

00:40:17.167 --> 00:40:19.001
Come on.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
